# env: HOME=home
# The table's `+ New session` chip (and `sessions.new_menu`) is the
# choice menu: a local session, one in a worktree of its own, the ×2 /
# ×4 / ×8 batches, and the two
# cloud wizards — which say so when the API is not configured rather
# than hide.

write home/.claude/projects/-tmp-ws/e2e00004-0000-4000-8000-000000004001.jsonl {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"write the release notes"}}\n{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Drafted them."}]}}
command sessions.table
wait 800
command sessions.new_menu
expect screen contains "New local session"
expect screen contains "New session in a worktree…"
expect screen contains "Open ×2"
expect screen contains "Open ×8"
expect screen contains "New cloud run… (not configured)"
expect screen contains "New cloud run (wizard)… (not configured)"
key esc
expect screen lacks "New local session"
